@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] actor-owned-state-boundaries
Production code outside a domain owner MUST request state changes through that owner's explicit
command interface or documented synchronous API. It MUST NOT mutate actor-owned state directly or
move business validation into handles or Tauri adapters.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] runtime-events-are-facts
Production `AppEventBus` events MUST report facts that have occurred, never request work. Requests
MUST use the owning domain's command interface, and diagnostics that do not represent application
state MUST use `tracing` instead of the event bus.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:safety] generation-scoped-stale-work
Code holding shared generation authority MUST treat a rejected generation check as terminal for the
operation. It MUST NOT then send LV1 commands, mutate current or app-lifetime state, or publish or
log success, and stale work MUST NOT affect a newer runtime.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] generation-tagged-fact-filtering
Generation-scoped LV1 and Fade actors MAY publish facts without reading shared generation authority,
but every such fact MUST carry the actor's assigned generation. Consumers of generation-bound state
MUST discard facts that do not match their active generation.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] projector-only-frontend-state
The projector MUST be the only backend component that constructs `AppViewState` snapshots and MUST
publish them through its host-neutral latest-value sink. Host adapters MAY forward those snapshots
to their UI event mechanism but MUST NOT construct snapshots or implement domain policy.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:security;logging] diagnostic-data-minimization
Production tracing and frontend-safe errors MUST NOT include credentials, tokens, raw OSC payloads,
or serialized or debug-formatted `AppSettings`, `PersistedSettings`, `ShowFile`, or `SessionDocument`
values. User-facing messages MUST remain understandable without structured diagnostic fields.
